Build option MESEN_CLOCK_START: a cartridge's clock with no saved clock
starts at the host's time of day, not at a fixed date.

Mesen's clocks start from a fixed point when the cartridge has no saved
clock: the S-3511A of the Game Boy Advance and WonderSwan cartridges at
2000-01-01 00:00:00, the Game Boy's MBC3 clock at 00:00:00 on day 0, and the
SPC7110's RTC-4513 at nothing a game takes for a date (all zeros). With this
option each starts at the time of day the host gives (MesenVirtualClockMs,
patch 0009), which Chimera's core sets from a project's Clock Start: the
S-3511A and the RTC-4513 at that date and time (the year's last two digits,
as the chips hold them), the MBC3 clock at that time of day, its day counter
at 0 (it holds no date). At 2000-01-01 00:00:00 the S-3511A and the MBC3
clock start as they did; the RTC-4513 now starts at that date. A saved clock
is loaded as before. New file Core/Shared/Utilities/ClockStart.h works the
date out without the C library. Off, nothing changes.

